1.40    Threaded state (${state}): a value of your own that flows left to
          right along each parse path, like ${scope}.  Speculative actions
          read and replace it; paths whose states differ are kept apart, so
          it can decide which parses are accepted.  ${state N} is the state
          before element N.  D_Parser.state_fns (D_StateFns) interns states
          and can prefer between parses ending with different states;
          whitespace functions read it with d_get_whitespace_state.  Also
          d_get_state, d_get_state_before and d_intern_state.  C++:
          Parser::set_state<T>, dparser::make_state / dparser::state.
          Python: a `state` action argument, parse(initial_state=,
          prefer_state=).  Rust: StateId, Parser::make_state / state,
          initial_state, prefer_state and white_space_state_fn.
        Attributes after parsing: synthesized and inherited attributes on
          the saved tree, evaluated on demand, cached, copied down to
          descendants when a parent has no equation, and checked for
          cycles.  C: dattr.h (d_attr_tree, d_attr_get, ...), part of
          libdparse.  C++: dattr.hpp (dparser::Attr<T>, syn, inh,
          AttrTree).  Python: the dparser_attrs module (@syn, @inh) and
          parse(keep_tree=True) with ParsedStructure.getTree() and Node.
          Rust: dparser::attrs.
        d_get_production: the rule that built a node.  make_dparser -H 1
          writes D_RULE_<production>_<n> constants; with -a they go to the
          actions file and build_actions makes them Rust constants.  Rust:
          ParseNode::production().
        D_Parser has two new fields at the end: recompile code that uses
          dparse.h.  Rust ParseNode has new fields state and state_before.
        python.g and tests/python.test.g keep the bracket depth and the
          indentation stack in ${state} instead of $g, and no longer need
          ${declare mutable_speculative_globals}.  Misindented code is now
          a syntax error, tabs indent correctly, and python.g treats match
          and case as soft keywords.  Each statement's tree has a new
          first child, LINE.
        make test also runs the C++, Python grammar and threaded state
          tests.

1.39    BREAKING: $g is read-only in speculative actions: a
          const D_ParseNode_Globals * in C and C++, a &G in Rust, so writes
          no longer compile. Add ${declare mutable_speculative_globals} to
          restore the old behavior.
        Rust: a new runtime, ported from the C engine, which parses as C
          does (same trees, disambiguation, error recovery and statistics
          on the C test suite): speculative actions with ${reject}, the
          symbol table (${scope}, ${parser}.symtab), passes, error
          recovery, whitespace productions, external scanners and
          whitespace functions (Parser::with_actions), start symbols,
          partial parses, the commit interval, ambiguity_fn and all of the
          C options.
          BREAKING: actions get the node as $n (children as its children)
          and their globals separately; ambiguity_fn sees the alternatives
          before their final actions run; an unresolved ambiguity fails the
          parse; syntax errors are recovered from and reported.
        make_dparser -B -a: write speculative, final and pass code with
          their kind; give rules the `_` default actions; record external
          scanners and whitespace functions instead of failing; expand
          ${nterm}, ${string} and ${pass}; fix binary tables for grammars
          with terminal actions, defaults or passes.
        Regenerate the bootstrap grammar parser (grammar.g.c).

1.38    Symbol table: fix commit_D_Scope breaking later updates; add
          SPECULATIVE_NEW_D_SYM so declarations don't leak between parse
          paths; keep tied derivations with different symbol tables apart.
        dparse() no longer reads past buf_len; input need not be
          NUL-terminated.
        C++ wrapper: no crash without save_parse_tree; trees are freed
          completely; save_parse_tree defaults to on.
        Install read_binary.h and dparse.hpp; add public D_ASSOC_* values
          for external scanners.
        CMake: install all headers, make find_package(dparser) work, fix
          the version.
        Python: restore start_symbol, make_token, print_debug_info and the
          g argument; getStringLeft() returns the unparsed input, new
          getString() returns the (possibly edited) parsed text.
        Rust: flatten repetitions, don't drop the last character, reject
          incomplete input, exclude trailing whitespace from node text.
        Documentation site at https://jplevyak.github.io/dparser/

